+## OpenHarmony Support
+
+This source tree carries an OpenHarmony/OHOS libc and compiler adaptation for
+`aarch64-linux-ohos`, `arm-linux-ohoseabi`, and `x86_64-linux-ohos`. A Zig
+compiler built from this repository can cross-compile applications for all
+three targets; the target passed to the top-level `build` script is still the
+host platform on which the Zig compiler itself will run.
+
+The reproducible maintenance, package, and full-system QEMU test workflow is
+documented in [ohos/README.md](ohos/README.md). In particular:
+
+```sh
+# Build and package a host Zig distribution containing OHOS support.
+scripts/ohos/build-package.sh
+
+# Compile and run the OHOS matrix in harmony-contrib/ohos-qemu images.
+scripts/ohos/test-qemu.sh --zig out/host/bin/zig \
+  --packages /path/to/ohos-qemu/artifacts --arch all
+```
+
+Pinned source revisions, QEMU artifact names, and SHA-256 values are recorded
+in `ohos/manifest.json`.
+
